 the bunch is  between Tyrion and Cersei there's so  much subtext to be mined from their  relationship due to their Rich history  together that makes every scene they  have very insightful and intriguing then  you can basically apply that fact to  every other dialogue scene because the  world of Game of Thrones is so layered  that you're constantly either learning  about the character or the world to some  degree from that character's perspective  making the story constantly riveting and  I haven't even gone into the masterful  Blackwater sequence that was perfectly  built up with great tension and rocking  a perfect execution of a spectacle and  gritty violence even with some of season  2 shortfalls and the fact that the plot  doesn't pop off as much as other Seasons  it still manages to be an excellent  season of Game of Thrones  season three now this is extremely hard  and I can honestly interchange any of  the next three seasons because of how  magnificent they all are but just barely  I'm going to put season 3 under seasons  one and four because those seasons are  essentially perfect the only flaws I  have was season 3 are the anticlimactic  Battle of yunkai Theon getting tortured  All Season became a little repetitive in  the King's Landing narrative to me is  weaker than the other three first  Seasons not saying it's bad in any way  and it's still really good the political  dance between Tywin and Elena as they  manipulate their children on its own is  amazing but to me the death of Ned Stark  the Blackwater and the chaos of season  four outshines that ever so slightly and  honestly we'll come down to preference  as to which one of those narratives is  your favorite but yeah those are really  the only negative things I can think of  because there are so many great aspects  to be enjoyed from the best scene in the  show of the right wedding Jaime losing  his hand and having his bath monologue  Danny acquiring the unsullied Tywin  exploding on his children and 