le for chicken  Daenerys seizing Marine Jon killing the  mutineers at craster's keep and  obviously Joffrey choking on some pie it  feels like every episode has an orgasmic  climax that sends my brain on a dopamine  parade then this is arguably some of the  best arcs for our characters like Tyrion  Arya and Jon Tyrion hits his lowest  point and nothing holds him back from  unleashing all his anger arya's Journey  with the Hound is a surprising Delight  as she slowly comes to grow a fondness  for him as a father figure of sorts the  fact that the Hound even shares the  sentiment by the end marks a great end  point for his overall character Arc and  then Jon has a massive moral dilemma in  which she has to protect his brothers  from the wildlings despite him actually  agreeing with their cause and having  personal stakes in them with egrets this  isn't even mentioning that the Watchers  on the walls in this season which is by  far my favorite episode in the show some  of the best action dialogue set pieces  and heart-wrenching character moments  can be found in this episode I feel like  I can start any episode in this season  and immediately become entranced by the  immense quality that each one has I love  season 4 and there might be a couple of  small flaws here and there like the  terrible editing and the Hound and  brienne's fight scene but the story  Peaks here on almost every front to the  point that they don't matter thank you  for watching and let me know in the  comments what your ranking of the  seasons is
 

